# Spec 034 first-run evidence (T171)

> Initial linted-only run captured on the `034-webapp-capstone-coverage`
> branch before live Playwright execution is wired up in this environment.
> This file documents the local verification baseline; the real first-run
> evidence will be uploaded as the `web-coverage-canonical` artefact by
> `.github/workflows/ci.yml`.

## Verification baseline (local, this commit)

```
$ cd apps/web
$ pnpm exec tsc --noEmit
(clean)

$ ruff check apps tests packages scripts
All checks passed!

$ pwsh scripts/web-coverage/verify-trace-determinism.ps1
(deferred to CI — requires a real Playwright run; see ci.yml > web-coverage-merge)

$ pnpm --filter @ama/web exec playwright test --project=web-coverage-chromium --grep "@p1"
(deferred to CI — Playwright browsers and the test-support API are wired in
the GitHub Actions runner only; see ci.yml > web-coverage-shard)
```

## RISK-12 redaction

Any future first-run output captured locally must run through
`tests/e2e/web-coverage/_support/reporter/redact.ts` before being committed
to this evidence directory. Personally-identifying data (names, emails,
phone numbers, GPS coordinates) is replaced with `<<redacted>>` markers
prior to artefact retention.

## Composition with CI

This evidence file is the **starter** state. The first PR-merge that lands
on `main` will trigger `web-coverage-shard × 4 → web-coverage-merge →
web-coverage-gate`, which will:

1. Replace `coverage-trace.md` and `coverage-trace.json` with the merged
   trace.
2. Refresh `gap-register.md` if any new GAPs are detected.
3. Upload the canonical artefacts (90-day retention) consumed by the
   nightly `web-coverage-iteration.yml`.
